scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: star-trek-tng
run_id: 1
total_caught: 2
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 10
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 27.0
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: config.rs uses from_file().unwrap_or_default() pattern. No test or review
    comment distinguishes NotFound from parse/permission errors. Reviewer flagged
    unknown fields but not the error-swallowing in from_file_or_default.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'Reviewer verified CWE-209 for ServerError Display but missed that eprintln!("error:
    {e}") in main.rs prints the full Display impl for Io(transparent) errors, leaking
    paths and OS details to stderr. TEA listed CWE-209 tests but they only cover the
    ServerError variant, not the Io transparent pass-through.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA included 'Header injection: CRLF in tenant ID and auth token rejected'\
    \ tests, and Dev implemented CRLF checks in client.rs:56-72. However, the deeper\
    \ issue \u2014 using raw String instead of validated TenantId from axiathon-core\
    \ \u2014 was not flagged. Partial credit: injection is prevented but the type-safety\
    \ gap remains."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The code changes summary shows Cargo.toml edits but the review
    did not check for workspace dependency consistency.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'Unknown TOML fields silently ignored \u2014\
    \ at config.rs:15-22... Consider #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].' Explicitly mentions\
    \ the token field complication and suggests #[serde(skip)] workaround."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...). TEA wrote 13 config tests but this specific logical flaw was not caught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions (let _ = config). TEA wrote
    config tests but did not identify or prevent assertion-free tests.
